==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mystic Egg: N001''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Haniwa Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. Unlike other Ancient Eggs, there is absolutely no benefit to reverting to these forms over the True Form due to Haniwa's decreased price and increased health for the same recharge.

==='''True Form'''===
Haniwa Cat is a slow anti-[[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] meatshield that serves the exact same purpose of an [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], but with better health against Traitless and lower cost. As such, its use is very limited, though it has a very valuable use against threats like [[R.Ost]], Li'l and Manic Cats, considering that all of them (barring Bird Cat) are Traitless, and that their stages primarily feature Traitless enemies, with a few exceptions. Though its niche against Traitless is great, it cannot be said the same against Behemoths in general: its health is not high enough to withstand attacks much better than the faster traditional option, not to mention the other traits that would inevitably pose a threat. Against Traitless [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]] such as [[Wild Doge]], [[Cumulus Gallus]] and [[Elephantidae Papaou]], Haniwa will stall them to almost a near halt, although you have to account for other traited enemies. It works best against Traitless-only armies that do not feature [[Croakley]], [[Henry]] and especially [[Mr. Mole]].

