==Trivia==
*Haniwa Cat is based on a ''[[wikipedia:Haniwa|haniwa]]'', which were clay statues that were buried with the dead.
**Since it attacks by spinning, it could also be a reference to the ''haniwa''-like [https://nookipedia.com/wiki/Gyroid gyroids] from the ''Animal Crossing'' series; the name "Gyroid" is derived from the word ''gyrate'', meaning "rotate".
**Haniwa Cat may also be based on Cat Haniwa from [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]]' discontinued game [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULz5pEItBpI| Dig! Dig! HANIWA!]
*Before its True Form was added in Version 11.5, the last line of Mystic Egg: N001's English description said "What will happen when it hatches...?" instead of "Resistant to Traitless enemy attacks".
*Strangely, unlike the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], it and [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N005]]'s names did not have colons when they were first released. The colons were later added in [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]].
*This unit is the only Ancient Egg unit not to have its True Form when it was first added to the game.
*Visually, [[Haniwanwan]] is an enemy version of Haniwa Cat.
*Haniwa is the only unit to cost less than its egg.

